# [AVTCORE](../wg/avtcore.html)

## Summary

The Audio/Video Transport Core Maintenance and Extensions (AVTCORE) Working Group met at IETF 127. The session covered working group administration, updates on published RFCs and draft status, publication progress for active drafts, and technical presentations on payload formats, SFrame transport, Opus multistream SDP signaling, frame-level acknowledgements, and future payload format work for AV2.

## Key Discussion Points

### Administration and Working Group Status
- **Chairs:** Jonathan Lennox, Marius Curelea
- **Presentation:** [AVTCore IETF 127 Chair Slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-avtcore-avtcore-ietf-127-chair-slides-00)
- **Status:**
  - Published RFC 10034 (V3C Payload Format).
  - JPEG XS and Green Metadata payload formats are currently in the RFC Editor Queue.
  - The working group discussed the status of `draft-ietf-avtcore-abs-capture-time` (Absolute Capture Time RTP Header Extension). Aaron Rosenberg explained that it adds an NTP capture timestamp per frame into an RTP header extension for playback synchronization. Jonathan Lennox noted that work stalled after the original author stepped away. The chairs will ask the mailing list whether there is interest to continue or park the document.

